no), we use the actual letters as the names of these dynamic elements. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other-dynamics element allows other dynamic marks that are not covered here. Dynamics elements may also be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"combined to create marks not covered by a single element, such as sfmp."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDynamics","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldynamics"]}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDynamics/valign":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The valign attribute is used to indicate vertical alignment to the top, middle, bottom, or baseline of the"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"text. Defaults are implementation-dependent.","type":"text"}],"title":"valign","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"valign","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLValign","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLValignO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldynamics\/valign","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDynamics\/valign"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDynamics":{"abstract":[{"text":"Dynamics can be associated either with a note or a general musical direction. To avoid inconsistencies between","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and among the letter abbreviations for dynamics (what is sf vs. sfz, standing alone or with a trailing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dynamic that is not always piano), we use the actual letters as the names of these dynamic elements. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other-dynamics element allows other dynamic marks that are not covered here. Dynamics elements may also 